  "title": "Daily Report - 2026-07-02",
  "categories": [
    {
      "title": "ElizaOS Token Utility, Plugin Updates, and Community Discussion",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "A discussion arose in the community regarding a code change (issue #10732) that sets USDC as the default payout asset instead of the elizaOS token. A community member raised concerns that this change could reduce elizaOS token utility and eliminate buybacks. Odilitime clarified that this change is specifically about payouts, not payments, and that paying out in elizaOS would likely cause businesses to dump the token, making USDC a safer and potentially better option for the ecosystem. Odilitime further confirmed that elizaOS remains one of the accepted crypto tokens for payments, and that USDC payouts apply to the new cloud business services. The clarification was well received by the community.",
          "sources": [
            "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1253563209462448241"
          ],
          "images": [],
          "videos": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A community member shared a Twitter Space link featuring Ruby Trivia speaking on an AMA about vibe-coded games hosted by Looplay, discussing whether we are entering a golden age of that genre.",
          "sources": [
            "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1253563209462448241"
          ],
          "images": [
            "https://abs.twimg.com/sticky/cards/TwitterSpacesCardImage.3.jpg"
          ],
          "videos": []
        },
        {
          "text": "GBLIN announced the release of plugin-gblin version 0.2.4 for Eliza agents. The update introduces a new action called GET_GBLIN_RISK_ATTESTATION, which allows an agent to pay $0.003 via x402 in USDC on Base gaslessly and receive a 10-minute EIP-712-signed proof of the current BTC/ETH risk regime. The proof can be attached to subsequent agent actions and verified by any counterparty for free. The plugin also includes treasury health checks, the ability to park idle USDC into an on-chain index, and JIT-swaps back to USDC for invoice payments, totaling 4 actions and 1 provider all running against live Base mainnet. The developer invited feedback from anyone running trading or treasury agents.",
          "sources": [
            "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1253563209462448241"
          ],
          "images": [],
          "videos": []
        },
        {
